Q: How to typecheck x.startswith() when x has type str | bytes? A: <p>You can move the <code>startswith</code> check into the <code>if</code> block:</p>
<pre class="lang-py prettyprint-override"><code>import json
from typing_extensions import Any

import lz4.block

bytebuf = bytes | bytearray
MAGIC_HEADER = b&quot;mozLz40\0&quot;


def jsonlz4_loads(buf: str | bytebuf) -&gt; Any:
    if isinstance(buf, bytebuf):
        header = MAGIC_HEADER
        is_valid = buf.startswith(header)
    else:
        header = MAGIC_HEADER.decode(&quot;ascii&quot;)
        is_valid = buf.startswith(header)

    if not is_valid:
        raise ValueError(&quot;Not a valid JSONLZ4 buffer - magic bytes missing&quot;)

    return json.loads(lz4.block.decompress(buf[len(header):]))
</code></pre>
<p>It is not as DRY but it gets rid of the type checking errors.</p>
